{
  "_comment": "The one list of Craft apps and ecosystems. Read by src/ecosystems/catalog.ts (workspace), scripts/fetch-apps.mjs, scripts/check-versions.mjs and scripts/releases.mjs (builds). Versions are NOT here: they live in public/releases.json (the office apps) and public/web-builds.json (the others, written by npm run apps:fetch or apps:import). To add an app: one entry here (and its id in CRAFT_IDS of catalog.ts, which a test keeps equal), an icon in public/assets/craft/<id>.png, then npm run apps:fetch. origin: artcraft = made by the ArtCraft team, community = a community app the ArtCraft launcher lists, independent = a third-party app of independent developers. license is the SPDX id of the app (a GPL app is fetched on the user's machine, never committed, and its licence is shown). channel: release = the repository publishes a web zip (asset, default -web-*.zip) that apps:fetch installs; pages = the app is deployed on GitHub Pages (pages = its URL) and apps:fetch mirrors that site (scripts/mirror-pages.mjs); source = no web release and no Pages app: only built from source (the upstream collection compiles it with patches): apps:fetch cannot get it, but a build folder <id>-web-<version>/ dropped into versions/ is imported like any other. File types come from workcraft-ai crates/agents/src/craft/spec.rs and the opens/imports lists of independent developers tools.yaml; opens = the formats the app is the natural home for, imports = everything else it reads.",
